# Mobile Application Security

## Secure Storage

- **iOS:** Use Keychain with `kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly` for sensitive data
- **Android:** Use EncryptedSharedPreferences or Android Keystore — **never** plain SharedPreferences for secrets
- **React Native:** Use `react-native-keychain` — **never** AsyncStorage for tokens
- **Flutter:** Use `flutter_secure_storage`
- **Never** hardcode API keys in source — use build-time injection via environment variables
- Set `android:allowBackup="false"` to prevent unencrypted backup exposure
- Disable verbose logging in production builds

## Network Security

- Implement certificate pinning for API connections (pin to leaf or intermediate cert)
- **Android:** Set `cleartextTrafficPermitted="false"` in `network_security_config.xml`
- **iOS:** Don't set `NSAllowsArbitraryLoads: true` — enforce ATS (App Transport Security)
- **Never** disable TLS verification (`InsecureSkipVerify`, `TrustManager` accepting all certs)
- **Never** send tokens or PII in URL path/query parameters

## Authentication

- Use biometric auth to unlock Keychain/Keystore-stored credentials, then authenticate with server
- Implement silent token refresh — handle 401 by refreshing before retrying
- Require biometric/PIN re-verification for sensitive operations (payment, profile changes)
- Clear credentials on first launch after reinstall

## Binary Security

- **Android:** Set `debuggable false`, enable R8/ProGuard, use release signing
- **iOS:** Use Swift whole-module optimization
- Implement app attestation: Play Integrity API (Android), App Attest (iOS)
- Set `exported="false"` for internal Android Activities/Services

## WebView Security

- Disable JavaScript when not needed in WebViews
- Set `setAllowFileAccess(false)` and `setAllowFileAccessFromFileURLs(false)`
- Minimize `addJavascriptInterface` exposure — validate origin
- Block mixed content: `setMixedContentMode(MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW)`

## Deep Links

- Use App Links (Android) / Universal Links (iOS) with domain verification — not custom URL schemes
- Validate all deep link parameters against allowlists
- **Never** pass credentials or PII in deep links
- Validate redirect destinations against trusted domains
